Here's an updated script that uses cursor-based pagination:
```java
function getShopifyOrders() {
  var shop_url = 'YOUR_SHOP_URL';
  var access_token = 'YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN';

  var start_date = new Date();
  start_date.setMonth(start_date.getMonth() - 1);
  var end_date = new Date();

  var url = 'https://' + shop_url + '/admin/api/2023-03/orders.json?created_at_min=' + start_date.toISOString() + '&created_at_max=' + end_date.toISOString() + '&status=any&fields=order_number,customer,subtotal_price,total_price,created_at,shipping_address,shipping_lines,source_name,location_id,total_tax,financial_status';

  var headers = {
    'X-Shopify-Access-Token': access_token
  };

  var options = {
    'method': 'get',
    'headers': headers
  };

  var sheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSheet();
  sheet.clearContents();
  sheet.appendRow(['Order Number', 'Customer Name', 'Subtotal', 'Total', 'Created At', 'Shipping Address Province', 'Shipping Line Title', 'Shipping Cost', 'Source', 'Location ID', 'Current Tax', 'Financial Status']);

  var orders = [];
  var has_next_page = true;
  var page_info = '';

  while (has_next_page) {
    var page_url = url + page_info;
    var response = UrlFetchApp.fetch(page_url, options);
    var page_data = JSON.parse(response.getContentText());

    orders = orders.concat(page_data.orders);
    has_next_page = page_data.hasOwnProperty('next_page');
    page_info = has_next_page ? '&page_info=' + page_data.next_page : '';
  }

  for (var i = 0; i < orders.length; i++) {
    var order = orders[i];
    var shipping_address_province = order.shipping_address ? order.shipping_address.province_code : '';
    var shipping_line_title = order.shipping_lines.length > 0 ? order.shipping_lines[0].title : '';
    var shipping_cost = order.shipping_lines.length > 0 ? order.shipping_lines[0].price : '';
    var order_source = order.source_name ? order.source_name : '';
    var location_id = order.source_name === 'pos' ? order.location_id : '';
    sheet.appendRow([order.order_number, order.customer.first_name + ' ' + order.customer.last_name, order.subtotal_price, order.total_price, order.created_at, shipping_address_province, shipping_line_title, shipping_cost, order_source, location_id, order.total_tax, order.financial_status]);
  }
}
```
In this updated script, we have replaced the `page` parameter with a `page_info` parameter in the URL, which includes a cursor that indicates the next page of results. We use a `while` loop to keep iterating over pages until there are no more pages left to retrieve.

Note that the new cursor-based pagination method may perform differently than the old page-based method, so you may want to monitor the script's performance and adjust as necessary.

